##
A book, and what a shelf can be asked about one.

Nothing here knows there is a lending desk. That is the point of putting it in a project of
its own: it can be built, read, and reused without the program that happens to use it today.

Public, because Library is meant to use it. A type written with no visibility reaches its own
project and no further, which is why Wording beside it stays inside Books however many
projects reference this one.
##

public model Book

    string title;
    string author;
    integer copies;

    public function Book(string title, string author, integer copies)
        this.title = title;
        this.author = author;
        this.copies = copies;
    end function

    public string function Title()
        yield this.title;
    end function

    public string function Author()
        yield this.author;
    end function

    public integer function Copies()
        yield this.copies;
    end function

    public boolean function IsAvailable()
        yield this.copies > 0;
    end function

    public function Lend()
        if this.copies <= 0
            throw new ArgumentException();
        end if

        this.copies = this.copies - 1;
    end function

    public string function Described()
        yield Wording.Join(this.title, this.author);
    end function

end model
